  "_ionosphereFree": "IONOSPHERE-FREE CODE twin of scene_G5S6R4_ts3600_TW1_inc.json. Identical except cfg.atmosphere.ionosphereFree=true, which ConfigFactory.applyAtmosphereProfile resolves to cfg.measurements.codeMode='ionosphereFree'. The base scenario runs codeMode='singleFrequency', so its CODE rows carry the full first-order ionosphere corrected only by Klobuchar (~50% effective); the CARRIER rows already run the IF combination in both. MEASURED effect of this one key at 600 s TW1: along-track 3.677 -> 1.181 m, cross-track 2.599 -> 0.986 m, radial -> 0.117 m. That is the 4-6 m along/cross floor that TW1 exposed once it removed the 20 m radial/clock error. SCENARIO CHOICE, not a bug fix: single-frequency code is realistic for a single-frequency uplink; ionosphere-free code assumes dual-frequency ground transmitters. Pair with the base scenario to see both.",
  "atmosphere": {
    "ionosphereFree": true
  }
